    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/acentrogobius_viridipunctatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>In nature, this fish lives in the lower parts of rivers and therefore likes some salt addition.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/acentrogobius_viridipunctatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>If the water is hard enough (from 10° dGH upwards), they also stay in perfect health in pure fresh water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/acentrogobius_viridipunctatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>It feeds on all usual types of frozen and live food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/acentrogobius_viridipunctatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>This goby is very peaceful, but breeding habits will be defended against intruders.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/acentrogobius_viridipunctatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Fully grown males have a very thick skull.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/acentrogobius_viridipunctatus_en/",
      "html": "<p>In breeding mood, the fish become completely black in base colour, on which the emerald spots contrast – an outstanding beautiful look that led to the popular name \"midnight goby\". Additionally, the bright band in the caudal fin becomes deep orange.</p>"
    }
